### IP address plan
Each region gets one `/16` per side (from `regions.yaml`). Pod ranges come from `100.64.0.0/10`, so the region `/16` is not consumed by pods. No hybrid connectivity exists, so non-RFC1918 pod ranges never leak.
Each region gets one `/16` per side (`cidr` in `regions.yaml`) and one `/13` per side for pods and services (`podCidr`, from `100.64.0.0/10`), so pods don't consume the region `/16`. No hybrid connectivity exists, so no
n-RFC1918 pod ranges never leak.

| Block inside the region /16 (e.g. non-prod `10.10.0.0/16`) | Use |
|---|---|
| `x.x.0.0/20` | `snet-gke-<region>`: node primary range for all of this side's clusters in the region |
| `x.x.16.0/19` | Service secondary ranges, `/22` per cluster (8 clusters) |
| `x.x.48.0/20` | `snet-run-<region>`: Cloud Run Direct VPC egress |
| `x.x.64.0/22` | `snet-mig-<region>`: MIG instances |
| `x.x.68.0/23` | Proxy-only subnet (regional internal ALB, regional Envoy) |
| `x.x.70.0/24` | `snet-ops-<region>`: runners, Ansible, management cluster nodes (hub region only) |
| `x.x.72.0/24` | PSC endpoints (Google APIs) |
| `x.x.96.0/19` | Private services access allocation (Cloud SQL) |
| `x.x.128.0/17` | Reserved for growth |
Every cluster has a **slot** (0-23) per region per side, recorded in `regions.yaml`, and gets its own subnet (decisions #23). Slot 0 is reserved for the management cluster.

| Pod ranges (`100.64.0.0/10`) | Allocation |
| Range (computed with `cidrsubnet`) | Use |
|---|---|
| Per region per side | one `/14` (non-prod from `100.64.0.0/12`, prod from `100.80.0.0/12`) |
| Per cluster | `/17` (max 64 pods per node → `/25` per node → 256 nodes per cluster), 8 clusters per region per side |
| `cidrsubnet(cidr, 8, slot)` → `/24` in `x.x.0.0/19` | `snet-<cluster>`: node range of that cluster (≤ 250 nodes) |
| `cidrsubnet(podCidr, 5, slot)` → `/18` | pod secondary range (64 pods/node → `/25` per node → 128 nodes) |
| `cidrsubnet(cidrsubnet(podCidr, 2, 3), 7, slot)` → `/22` | service secondary range (1,024 services) |
| `x.x.32.0/20` | `snet-run-<region>`: Cloud Run Direct VPC egress |
| `x.x.48.0/22` | `snet-mig-<region>`: MIG instances |
| `x.x.52.0/23` | Proxy-only subnet (regional internal ALB) |
