Design choices made during the build

None of these changes a locked decision. Each is recorded in docs/decisions.md (#23–25) or architecture §20 (C13–C17):
- One subnet per cluster. A subnet allows only 30 secondary ranges, which would have capped a region at 15 clusters.
- Three extra states per customer: keys-nonprod, keys-prod and exchange. The Dev/Stage key ring serves two environments, and the exchange resources sit in their own perimeter, so neither fits in a single per-environment state.
- DR failover is a reviewed Git change. DR backends sit at capacity 0 until a PR sets drActive for the cell. Before the database replica is promoted, the DR side would be serving from a read-only copy.
- Edge states own the load balancers. One state per group (one per region for Dev/Stage) owns everything on the LB, built from Git. That's because a single URL map can't be shared by 200 customer states.
- An IaC seed project made by L0, outside the 12 fixed projects, holds the Terraform state and identities.
- Two added VPC-SC rules let the Terraform identities administer L1 and the exchange perimeter.

