6. ArgoCD: no manual step

Once the merge lands, each instance's root Application picks up the new files.
1. Root chart: creates the customer's ArgoCD project, limited to its namespaces on its placed clusters, including the DR cluster.
2. Tenant ApplicationSet: creates tenant-<id>-<env> per environment (plus -dr in prod). It deploys helm/tenant: namespace, quota, storage class, network policies, Istio policies and per-product service accounts.
3. Product ApplicationSet: creates <id>-<product>-<env> (plus -dr). It deploys helm/product-base:
   - the migration Job runs first (primary cluster only)
   - then the Rollout: canary in uat and prod, rolling in dev and stage, minimum replicas on the DR cluster unless the customer chose hot standby
4. Cloud Run and MIG products: these get no ArgoCD Application. L3 created their services and MIGs. From then on the delivery step deploys their versions; that pipeline is built in Phase 4.

