## Onboarding a customer

A customer is onboarded with one pull request that sets only `region.primary`. That works only on top of
a platform that already exists. The steps below are what must be in place first, then the sequence that
runs for every new customer.

### What must exist before the first customer (one-time, platform team)
| # | Prerequisite | Created by | Why the customer needs it |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | GCP organization, billing account, org admin; public DNS domain delegated to Cloud DNS | Manual (assumptions in the brief) | Everything is created under the org; customer hostnames live in the public zone |
| 1 | IaC seed project, Terraform state bucket, Terraform identities (`tf-l1`, `tf-nonprod`, `tf-prod`), workload identity pool with GitHub and Bitbucket providers | **L0**: `infrastructure/layers/L0-bootstrap/bootstrap
.sh` (org admin, once) | Pipelines authenticate without keys and keep state remotely |
| 2 | GitHub repository settings: branch protection on `main`, CODEOWNERS teams, Environments `tf-<pool>` (with reviewers) and `tf-<pool>-readonly`, `deliver-*`, `promote-*`, `isolation-*`, and variables (`GCP_WIF_PROVI
DER`, `TF_STATE_BUCKET`, `TF_SERVICE_ACCOUNT`, `DEPLOYER_SERVICE_ACCOUNT`, ...) | Repository admin (settings, not code) | Merges are reviewed and every apply gets the right identity and approval |
| 3 | The 12 fixed projects, Shared VPCs, org policies, VPC-SC perimeters, Artifact Registries, Binary Authorization, platform identities (promoter, seed publisher/importer, ArgoCD), management clusters, **3 ArgoCD inst
ances with their root Applications** | **L1**: `infrastructure/layers/L1-foundation` (platform PR; GitHub-hosted for the first apply) | The customer's resources go into these projects and perimeters; ArgoCD delivers its
 Kubernetes objects |
| 4 | Self-hosted runner pools per environment group (devstage, uat, prod), registered to GitHub and Bitbucket | **L1** `runner-pools` + runner registration | Applies run inside the VPC-SC perimeters, which GitHub-hoste
d runners cannot reach |
| 5 | An **active region pair** in `inventory/regions.yaml` with cells: per group a GKE cluster (prod plus its DR cluster), Cloud SQL instances (prod plus DR replica), platform keys, the database bootstrap job, the seed
 work bucket; `inventory/clusters/` and `inventory/sql/` written back | **L2 region**: `infrastructure/layers/L2-region/<region>/<group>` (capacity or region PR) | Placement can only pick from cells that exist and have
headroom |
| 6 | Platform add-ons on every cluster: Istio ingress/egress gateways, Argo Rollouts, cert-manager, Falco, canary analysis, label admission policy | ArgoCD root Applications (automatic once the cluster is registered) |
 Tenant and product releases need the gateways, CRDs and policies |
| 7 | Load balancers, Cloud Armor policies and DNS zones per group (initial apply, no customers yet) | **L2 edge**: `infrastructure/layers/L2-edge/*` | Customer host rules and certificates are added to these |
| 8 | Catalog entries for the products the customer selects, their Helm values (GKE) and, for prod pins, **promoted digests** in `products/<p>/releases.yaml` | Platform + product teams (catalog PR); `promote-image.yml`
| The validator rejects unknown products, versions outside the window and unpromoted prod pins |

